repository-code: 'https://github.com/muhammedsara/eew-system'
abstract: >-
  A crowd-sourced earthquake early warning system that fuses a dense population
  of consumer smartphones with a sparse grid of fixed IoT anchors. Each sensor
  runs a 188 KiB INT8 CNN locally and transmits an 87-byte authenticated digest;
  a regional gateway applies a six-phase weighted spatio-temporal consensus that
  tests inter-sensor delay against inter-sensor distance and weights each sensor
  by the reliability it demonstrates in the field. The repository contains the
  protocol, the deployed detector and the full evaluation pipeline, so that every
  published number can be reproduced from a clone.
keywords:
  - earthquake early warning
  - edge intelligence
  - sensor fusion
  - distributed consensus
  - spatio-temporal graph
  - sensor reliability
  - crowdsensing
